SWEET WLAN stage 3 run A (patch 0129, W-D3 step 2, docs/research/43 rows W0..W7): the first chip WRITES from inside XNU, behind boot-arg sweetwlan=3 (stage 1 runs at level 2 first;
levels 1-2 are byte-identical to 0124/0128). Pure header bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_wr.h: deny-by-default tuple table swl_wt[] (+ read table swl_rt[], restore table swl_rs[]), the one writer swl_wr()
(level/predecessor/phase gate, the 0124 preconditions re-read, live window, old and companion value, store, read-back under the tuple's mask, STOP latch + restore of the armed group),
the run-A steps: entry state, outbound iATU region 2 over BAR2 (4 MiB) + its ml_io_map, SRPWR READ-ONLY check, SYS_MEM wrapper reset, 21 bank reads for the RAM size, CA7 halt, two BAR2 reads.
No image copy, no NVRAM, no ARM release: later runs are more rows in the tables. sweet_wlan.c glue: sw3_rd/sw3_wr (the one store, called only through swl_store()), needs ADT /sweet-wlan tcm and
atu-r2-off (tools/mkadt.py, soc.json wlan.tcm/tcm_bytes/atu_r2_off). Host test: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c, mutants: tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py. HW-WRITE path: NOT reviewed yet.

